'''Lin Gaava''' was a [[human]] [[Gender|female]] who lived during the [[New Republic Era|era]] of the [[New Republic]].<ref name="The Recruit" /> She worked as a [[Technician|mechanic]] on [[Jace Rucklin]]'s [[Rucklin's team|team]], on the ''[[Colossus]]'' platform on [[Castilon]]. Gaava had [[Color|red]] [[hair]], blue [[eye]]s, and light skin. After the [[Occupation of the Colossus|occupation]] of the ''Colossus'', she eventually joined the [[First Order]] as a [[First Order TIE fighter pilot|TIE pilot]] [[cadet]].

==Biography==
[[File:Colossus-Databank.jpg|thumb|right|250px|The ''Colossus'', where Lin Gaava lived during the late New Republic era.]]
Lin Gaava was a member of [[Jace Rucklin]]'s [[Rucklin's team|racing team]] during the [[New Republic era]], which included the [[Gender|male]] [[Sullustan]] [[Gorrak Wiles]]. They had a reputation as fun-loving troublemakers and idlers aboard the ''[[Colossus]]'' platform on the ocean world of [[Castilon]].<ref name="Fuel for the Fire" /> Gaava frequented the [[Colossus marketplace|''Colossus'' marketplace]] and docks.<ref name="The Recruit" /><ref name="Triple Dark">{{Resistance|The Triple Dark}}</ref>

===Exploiting Kaz===
[[File:RucklinsTeam-FuelForTheFire.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Lin Gaava joined Jace Rucklin's racing team alongside Gorrak Wiles.]]
Gaava and her associates Rucklin and Wiles encountered the undercover [[Resistance]] [[spy]] [[Kazuda Xiono]], who worked as a mechanic at [[Jarek Yeager]]'s [[Jarek Yeager's Repair Station|repair station]]. Taking advantage of Xiono's dissatisfaction with his demanding employer, Rucklin and his associates befriended Xiono, appealing to his love for racing and having fun. Lin also claimed that they were free to take leave anytime.<ref name="Fuel for the Fire" />

Gaava and Wiles later watched on the platform as Rucklin and Xiono raced on [[speeder bike]]s over the sea. Under Rucklin's instructions, Gaava and Wiles had sabotaged Xiono's speeder bike so that Rucklin could rescue him and gain Xiono's trust. Rucklin's plan worked, and he thanked Gaava and Wiles for their work.<ref name="Fuel for the Fire" />

[[File:JaceRucklinRacer-FuelForTheFire.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Lin and Gorrak were working on Rucklin's racer when Jace began manipulating Kazuda Xiono.]]
Later, Xiono visited [[Jace Rucklin's hangar]], where he found Gaava, Wiles, and Rucklin working on [[Rucklin's racer]]. Xiono had ignored his friend [[Neeku Vozo]]'s advice that Rucklin and his associates were little more than idlers and troublemakers. Gaava was stripping Rucklin's racer of "unnecessary" systems to reduce the ship's weight.<ref name="Fuel for the Fire" />

Rucklin then convinced Xiono to allow him to visit Yeager's trophy room so that he could steal a canister of [[Corellian]] [[Coaxium|hyperfuel]]. When Rucklin returned, Gaava and Wiles praised Rucklin for executing his heist. Lin also warned Ruckling to be careful as he poured hyperfuel into his racer's tank.<ref name="Fuel for the Fire" />

After Xiono discovered the theft, he returned to the hangar. Gaava and Wiles watched as Xiono remonstrated with Rucklin, who had already injected the hyperfuel into the racer's engines. Xiono managed to rescue an unwilling Rucklin, but his racer was destroyed. Lin and Wiles supported Rucklin when he chastised Xiono for destroying his ship. Xiono countered that Rucklin had stolen Yeager's hyperfuel, something which Rucklin denied.<ref name="Fuel for the Fire" />

===In the background===
[[File:TheSearchForKaz.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Lin was present at the ''Colossus'' marketplace while Resistance astromech BB-8 was searching for Kazuda.]]
While the [[BB-series astromech droid]] [[BB-8]] was searching for Xiono, Gaava was frequenting the ''Colossus'' marketplace.<ref name="The Search for Kaz">{{Resistance|The Search for Kaz}}</ref> During [[Kragan Gorr]]'s [[Warbird gang|Warbirds]]' [[Raid on the Colossus|second raid]] on the ''Colossus'', Gaava and Wiles took advantage of the chaos to salvage supplies from the marketplace.<ref name="Synara's Score">{{Resistance|Synara's Score}}</ref>
Gaava also frequented the ''Colossus'' marketplace, which was a familiar stomping ground of other ''Colossus'' residents including Neeku Voz, [[R1-J5|Bucket]], and Xiono.<ref name="Neeku's Reward">{{Resistance|Neeku's Reward}}</ref><ref name="Bucket's Quest">{{Resistance|Bucket's Quest}}</ref><ref name="Dangerous Business">{{Resistance|Dangerous Business}}</ref>

[[File:GalekAndCadets-LiveFire.png|thumb|right|250px|Following the First Order's occupation of the ''Colossus'', Lin joined the First Order Navy alongside Jace and Tamara Ryvora, undergoing fighter training with Lieutenant Galek.]]
Gaava continued frequenting the streets of the ''Colossus'' during the [[First Order]]'s [[Occupation of the Colossus|occupation]] of the platform.<ref name="The New Trooper">{{Resistance|The New Trooper}}</ref><ref name="The Disappeared">{{Resistance|The Disappeared}}</ref> Later, the First Order took an interest in Gaava and her friend Rucklin. While walking through the corridors of [[Doza Tower]], they crossed paths with [[First Order Security Bureau]] [[Agent]] [[Tierny]] and [[Tamara Ryvora]], whom Tierny was trying to recruit into the First Order.<ref name="No Escape Part 1">{{Resistance|No Escape: Part 1}}</ref> After joining the First Order alongside Rucklin and Ryvora, Gaava became a [[First Order TIE fighter pilot|TIE pilot]] [[cadet]], and participated in training exercises with them under the command of [[Lieutenant]] [[Galek]].<ref name="Live Fire" />

==Personality and traits==
Lin Gaava was a [[Gender|female]] [[human]] with red hair, blue eyes, and fair skin. Gaava and her associates had a reputation for laziness, humor, and playing pranks among the citizens of the ''Colossus''. Lin liked the fact that she and her colleagues could take days off and not work like droids. She and Wiles shared their leader Rucklin's willingness to steal and exploit his friendship with Xiono to advance Rucklin's racing ambitions. This included sabotaging Xiono's speeder bike so that Wiles could gain his trust.<ref name="Fuel for the Fire" />

As opportunists, Gaava and Wiles took advantage of a pirate raid on the ''Colossus'' to salvage supplies from the ''Colossus'' marketplace.<ref name="Synara's Score" />

==Skills and abilities==
Lin Gaava was a mechanic who was familiar with starships and speeder bikes.<ref name="Fuel for the Fire" />

==Behind the scenes==
Lin Gaava is a character created and developed for ''[[Star Wars Resistance]]''. She is voiced by [[Rachael MacFarlane]].<ref name="Fuel for the Fire credits">{{Resistance|Fuel for the Fire}} credits</ref>

